CICD Check

A Bash script that runs pre-release sanity checks on a Node.js project
(git state, dependencies, tests, Node versions and Dockerfile) and prints
a pass/fail report.

Requirements

-Bash 4+ (macOS ships 3.2: 'brew install bash')
-git, node, npm, and docker with the daemon running

Usage

    ./cicd-check.sh <command> [repo-path]

| Command                | Description                                  |
|------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| all                    | Run all checks (repo-path defaults to '.')   |
| help, -h, --help       | Show this README                             |
| version, -v, --version | Show the version                             |

Examples:

    ./cicd-check.sh all
    ./cicd-check.sh all ~/projects/my-app

Checks

| Check                     | Passes when                                                 |
|---------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| Tools exist               | git, node, npm and docker are installed                     |
| Working directory clean   | 'git status' shows no changes                               |
| Main branch               | Current branch is 'main', 'master' or 'release'             |
| npm audit                 | 0 vulnerabilities found*                                    |
| npm ci                    | Install succeeds with 0 vulnerabilities*                    |
| npm test                  | Tests exit with status 0                                    |
| Versions match            | 'node -v', '.nvmrc' and 'package.json' engines are identical |
| Docker                    | Dockerfile passes 'docker build --check'                    |

Only runs if the project has a `package-lock.json` or `npm-shrinkwrap.json`.

Notes

-npm ci deletes and reinstalls node_modules.
-Versions must match exactly, e.g. '.nvmrc' set to 'v22.23.4' and
  engines set to >=22.23.4. Ranges or aliases like 'lts/*' won't match.
-'docker build --check' only validates the Dockerfile; it doesn't build
  an image.
-The script always exits 0. To fail a CI step on any failed check:

      ./cicd-check.sh all | tee report.txt
      ! grep -q " test failed" report.txt
